#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:115
#: 4d8e4e6c0f9a4d4085a88bb68f96b49b
msgid "Parachute Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:117
#: 68b2f2196b2541a18a41c85e420a5c06
msgid "An option to force the release servo or relay to remain active forever (until reboot) once triggered. This used in high altitude situations where the servo or relay may be frozen due to extremely low temperatures, until lower altitude, and warmer temperatures allow operation. This can be enabled by setting the :ref:`CHUTE_OPTIONS<CHUTE_OPTIONS>` bit 0 high."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:119
#: 1db0fb1faad0422d868e04c2eb4f4a99
msgid "Setting bit 1 high of :ref:`CHUTE_OPTIONS<CHUTE_OPTIONS>` will not disarm the vehicle before releasing the chute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:122
#: e314c00fdcaf4c02823cf21cf4252b54
msgid "RC Disable/Enable of Parachute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:124
#: d5c1db00616c4415a4d8b1839c5c9130
msgid "You can disable or enable parachute release using an RC channel/switch: set an ``RCx_OPTION`` to 21. A high position enables parachute release; other positions disable it. If an ``RCx_OPTION`` is set to 23 (Parachute 3Pos), the low position disables parachute release, middle position enables operation, and a high will attempt to force release, as explained above, assuming the enabling conditions described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:127
#: 16187419d9b3426c8847ad67c8bead05
msgid "When will the parachute deploy?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:129
#: 9b71246511d24c7ea7b358c99f433a8a
msgid "Automatic parachute release can occur when the vehicle has lost attitude control and has begun falling. The following must all be true for a full 1 second for automatic release to trigger:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:131
#: 5f5bba8f59194e57962c162090591fd0
msgid "The motors are armed (Copter) or flying (Plane)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:132
#: 773453eaede540e5825844e806160788
msgid "The vehicle is not landed (Copter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:133
#: 6f871c68ea0a46dc89be865734210029
msgid "The vehicle is not in FLIP or ACRO flight mode (Copter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:134
#: d2679b709ec04ac283e94f04cd9670ff
msgid "the roll and/or pitch angle of the vehicle is 30 degrees off from the target lean angle (Copter only)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:136
#: 38a6f1eac34b40bd95c20cdc1efecc61
msgid "the barometer shows the vehicle is not climbing (excessive baro noise CAN prevent release in some cases) (Copter & Plane)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:137
#: 1ee6716ee30d43b4943bb60ebad487ea
msgid "the vehicle is above the :ref:`CHUTE_ALT_MIN <CHUTE_ALT_MIN>` altitude when loss of control is first detected (Copter only). In a fast descent, the actual release may occur below this altitude. A value of \"0\" disables this check."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:143
#: d55ecd6578ed4c0d93b8bf9b67c2a19a
msgid "Testing the chute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:145
#: d3a18bfa583c4167aad4ff144c7b298e
msgid "Depending upon the release mechanism a parachute deployment can be dangerous so please take care when performing these tests, removing the parachute and vehicle propellers as is appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:149
#: f5eb2c33131a402f8ac2b1f8b7648344
msgid "To test manual deployment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:151
#: 6dbf41f85c614807807e6ac29623170b
msgid "Enable parachute release, if using a switch to disable release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:152
#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:164
#: 8eeed13886a14c538c3bb5916792337e
#: 204463a70c3e4f4997acc834a2648961
msgid "Set the :ref:`CHUTE_ALT_MIN <CHUTE_ALT_MIN>` parameter to zero to disable the minimum altitude check"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:154
#: b479d94b107648e881d0a49f2aedee60
msgid "Arm the vehicle in stabilize mode and raise the throttle above minimum (disconnect motors or remove props) (not required for Plane)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:156
#: d3a2c1c04e06418c89e2cee79a920d7b
msgid "Use one of the above manual RC channel switch activation methods or use Mission Planner SERVO/RELAY tab to switch the release Relay, MAVLink command, or set the PWM of the release servo."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:158
#: d8f5c1ffc42a4e39bb7d1bf039c5fbd9
msgid "You should see the motors stop, the parachute release mechanism activate, and if telemetry is attached, \"Parachute: Released!\" should appear on the Flight Data screen's HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:162
#: 6c8e2cef997e4f0eac398a254cfa9cc5
msgid "To test the automatic deployment:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:166
#: dd8d0b9682bc4ad6971de1c5c9cfd582
msgid "Arm the vehicle in stabilize mode and raise the throttle above minimum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:168
#: 347c172c3d0b4f8fa210d8dce612642d
msgid "somehow tilt the vehicle over by at least 30 degrees while lowering it (the barometer shows the vehicle is descending)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:170
#: 12550962acf547e5a84fa47bc148b897
msgid "After 1 seconds, the motors should stop, the parachute servo will move and if Mission Planner is attached, \"Parachute: Released\" should appear on the Flight Data screen's HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-parachute.rst:174
#: 86a75621e3d046ba9f1e6b4736f0ed2b
msgid "After the test is complete, return the :ref:`CHUTE_ALT_MIN <CHUTE_ALT_MIN>` to the desired altitude (default is 10m)"
msgstr ""
